=================
1. tsn-delay-config

The tsn-delay-config executable needs to be run only once after every boot. This
application would read the delays in the mrphy ip from its registers using
the sysfs enteries provided.
This application after reading all the delays from mrphy ip, calculates the 
total Egress and Ingress delays and programs the same into the XGMAC register
again using the sysfs enteries provided.

This is required for applications like TSN and PTP.

The binary of this applications can be found in /home/root/tsn-delay-config

Usage of the application
--------------------------------
1. The application once executed as below, looks for all the eth interfaces containing the mrphy delay
   related sysfs parameters, reads these parameter values and then calculates and shows the values 
   programmed in the Egress and Ingress registers of XGMAC with a successfull message at the end.
   
   ./tsn-delay-config

